sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Client
  participant Guard as JWT/Roles Guard
  participant Service as Business service
  participant Idem as IdempotencyService
  participant Runner as TransactionRunner
  participant Locks as DataGuardsService
  participant DB as MongoDB replica set
  participant Worker as Outbox worker
  Note over Service,DB: EN-02 command contract; US-21 adds read-only lookup/preview. US-22 settlement is not implemented yet.
  Client->>Guard: GET /transactions or /transactions/:id (US-21)
  Guard->>Service: Current STAFF/ADMIN + allowlisted query
  Service->>DB: Read real GYM/PT transactions, sale/payment/invoice projections
  Service-->>Client: Page or detail + version, asOf; no key/hash/secret
  Client->>Guard: POST /transactions/:id/payment-preview + manual evidence (US-21)
  Guard->>Service: Current STAFF/ADMIN + PaymentReviewDto
  Service->>DB: Read current sale/amount/state, member eligibility, reference with simple collation
  Service-->>Client: READY / NEEDS_REVIEW / BLOCKED; canConfirm, blockingCodes, amountDue, asOf
  Note over Client,DB: Preview writes nothing and reserves nothing. READY is not SETTLED. Confirm must recheck under locks and unique indexes (US-22).
  Client->>Guard: Command + Bearer + UUID v4 Idempotency-Key
  Guard->>Service: Current principal, validated DTO
  Service->>Idem: execute(actorId, operation, key, normalized payload/target)
  Idem->>Runner: run(callback)
  Runner->>DB: withTransaction(snapshot, majority, primary, timeout 10s)
  Idem->>DB: Read own operation_requests using session
  alt Existing key, different hash
    Idem-->>Client: 409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT
  else Existing key, same hash
    Idem-->>Client: Original status/body after authentication
  else New intent
    Idem->>Service: work(session), may run again on transient errors
    Service->>Locks: acquire(session, ALL targets)
    Locks->>DB: Increment security_state → sorted plans → members → transactions
    Service->>DB: Read protected data, validate business rules in session
    Service->>DB: Write related business documents + notification/outbox in session
    Service-->>Idem: Allowlisted public DTO + result IDs
    Idem->>DB: Insert committed result using same session
    Runner->>DB: Commit all writes, or abort all on error
    Runner-->>Idem: Result / unknown commit outcome
    Idem-->>Client: Original result or 503 OPERATION_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN
    Worker->>DB: Claim committed outbox only
    Worker-->>Client: Realtime event after commit
  end
  Note over Client,DB: Duplicate operation key: abort losing transaction, retry same key within limits.
  Client->>Guard: GET /operations/:operation/:key
  Guard->>Idem: Current principal; ownership + operation role
  Idem->>DB: Read committed result by current actor
  Idem-->>Client: 200 COMMITTED or 404 OPERATION_UNKNOWN
  Note over Client: 404 may mean original request is still running. Keep the same key.
